let TEXT = "// lang/cie/world.eg — the world in Emerge (CIE-EG MOD-NATIVE-SYSTEM; Nexus phase CIE4_native_components, slice a): compartments, their state\n// and constraints, signals and handlers, the queue and its storm limit, rejection, spent, unrouted, and the hash-chained ledger with its\n// checkpoints, written through lang/cie/ledger.eg. The same behaviour and the same ledger, hash for hash, as lang/runtime.js.\n// James, 2026-11-06: \"Remove the last of the JavaScript\" · \"actaully keep remove js from emerge.\" · \"lets code what we can using emerge, that\n// way we can have a good test.\"\n// Runs interpreted and native (emerge.exe). The native compiler lowers compartment, component, contract, on, emit, send and wire to these\n// calls (lang/native/lower.eg, slices b and c).\n//\n//   start(seed, version, contract)       → genesis \{seed, version, chain_id, text[, contract, contract_hash]\}; contract: the raw block or null\n//   declare(spec)                        spec: \{name, id, state, constraints: [\{name, hard, cost, boundary, check: fn(view) → bool\}],\n//                                               handlers: [\{signal, run: fn(state, payload)\}]\}\n//                                        a component (slice c) also: component: true, namespace, version, ins: [\{name, shape, run\}],\n//                                               outs: [\{name, shape\}]; a shape is [\{name, type, nullable\}] or null\n//   send_in(comp, hook, payload) · emit_out(hook, payload) · connect(from, to, line) · roads(line)   ends: \{comp, hook\} or \{signal\}\n//   (send and wire are keywords, so the calls are send_in and connect)\n//   listen(signal, run)                    a top-level handler: run(payload)\n//   signal(name, payload)                 FIFO; from inside a handler, buffered until the handler commits\n//   state_of(name) · member_of(name, field) · spent() · unrouted() · entries() · verify()\n//   finish()                             the clean-shutdown check